WEBVTT

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.760
I can't remember what
happened after the battle.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.100
And yet...

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.230
Your Grace.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:35.070
Pardon me. I knocked many times,
but received no indication.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.740
Bring me wine. Enough to drown in.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:42.160
You've drunk enough.
It's more important that you eat--

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.750
That's an order!

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.750
But...

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.420
Why didn't you tell me?!
You must have known who he was!

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.840
With that same smile he gave me

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.640
and those hands he held me with,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.020
he ordered the death of York.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.680
And yet...

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.890
And yet, I...

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.650
York of the white rose.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.320
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.790
These royal houses with roses
for their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.420
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.600
How are Anthony's wounds?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.850
They aren't serious,

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.480
but I doubt he can fight
in the next battle.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.860
I see.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.820
And what of Richard?
He didn't attend the banquet.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.820
But I need him on the battlefield,
no matter what.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.080
I will check on him.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.950
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:28.870
Wait.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:35.420
Find the man who defied
my order and killed Warwick.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:39.170
I will punish whoever disobeyed his king.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.420
Count on it.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.340
Understood, Your Majesty.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.850
Why? Why did I meet him?

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.520
If we hadn't met that day,
at that time, then...

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.440
Hey!

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.530
What are you doing?

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.740
I committed the sin of disloyalty.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.960
And you want to punish yourself?

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.750
Kill me.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.420
Very well. I'll kill you.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:23.300
But if you die, York will lose.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:31.270
Listen, Richard. I'm not interested
in your inner turmoil,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.980
but you're the cornerstone of our army.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:40.900
If you really want to die, consider that
you just did, and this is hell.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.490
So...

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.200
You may remain mad.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.660
Merely slay the enemies before you.
Think of nothing else.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.580
Go on killing, Richard.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.000
That is my...

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.500
...my punishment.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.380
Father.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:12.100
I thought I understood that it
was an honor to die in battle.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:18.060
But I convinced myself that York
would spare my father in the end.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.110
It's no honor to die in battle.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.030
When you die, everything ends.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:27.820
George turned traitor
and your father was killed.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.120
There's no mercy in the House of York.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.870
I'll be blunt: Warwick's death
has made our victory uncertain.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:44.210
That said, I will not retreat.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:50.850
The Yorkists' goal isn't to drive us off;
it's the annihilation of Lancaster.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.810
Why tell me that?

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:58.980
I married into this country
from France when I was 15.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.570
The court manipulated the unstable Henry.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:06.360
It was a writhing nest of demons
determined to ensnare me.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.820
I've never once loved Henry.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.790
God took the man I truly loved.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.790
But I still have Edward.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.130
Anne, you're a kind girl,

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.710
so I suppose you've begun to love Edward.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:31.720
Don't let York take that child's life.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.140
As long as my boy Edward lives,

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:41.020
Lancaster can rise from the ashes.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:45.940
But what can I do?
Once the fighting starts--

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.030
Don't let him fight.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:56.540
I can't say any more myself.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:02.000
Do you understand, Anne?
This is not an order.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.050
I'm going to put Edward's
life in your hands.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.260
Lords! Lend me your ears!

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:14.720
Your sovereign, Henry, is now a prisoner.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:20.140
His authority has been usurped and his
lands turned to execution grounds!

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:24.190
Oh, my tears threaten to rob me of speech.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.230
The Earl of Warwick
was our anchor. I admit it.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.360
But what of that?

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.410
Though our mast may be
broken and our anchor gone,

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.330
I am still here!

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.370
As is the prince of the blood royal!

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.410
Muster your courage!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.710
In God's name!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:48.380
You who love the red rose,
march forth to victory!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:57.760
Gentlemen, I take it
you're prepared for war?

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.350
This is the moment I've been waiting for!

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.310
Bring my horse!

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.860
Wave the bloody flag!

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.690
It's victory or an honorable death!

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.000
I want to rush out this instant

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.170
and strike down fully
armored Yorkist soldiers!

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:35.640
Edward, run away now.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.930
What do you mean?

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:40.810
I've picked out a double to take
your place on the battlefield.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.020
Are you mad? You must be joking.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.150
It's to guard the blood of Lancaster!

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.900
I...

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:55.410
I thought that you, at least,
would understand how I feel.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:09:00.200
If you lose, the Yorkists will kill you.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:03.000
They even killed my father.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.170
And my mother and Isabelle
aren't with me anymore.

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.710
You're the only family I have.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.510
If we win this battle...

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:17.050
No, I'm certain we'll win.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.890
It will go down in history as
the first battle of a great king.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:27.730
You're, well... the first
friend I've ever had.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.320
Believe in me.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:34.530
I doubt I'll be able to sleep tonight.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.570
Shall we play chess?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.870
It will be practice for tomorrow's battle.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.960
I'm so sorry, Edward.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:54.670
Behold, Queen Margaret.
This places the foe downhill from us.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:10:00.600
What's more, they'll be forced to array
themselves amid brush and briars.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.890
Well done. I leave the command
entirely in your hands.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:07.310
But what of the crown prince?

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.600
The prince is still young.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:14.150
I've instructed him to obey
and learn from you.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.150
Haven't I, Edward?

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.990
Damn Lancaster!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.990
I didn't expect such a
well-arranged formation.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.830
But we surpass them in morale.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.450
And in number of cannons,
according to reports.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.500
But they have more men!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.540
Your Majesty.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:35.050
I have a plan.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:54.270
Warriors who bear the sign
of the white rose,

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:59.360
the time to put an end to
this long war has come at last!

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.030
Do not forget the wounds we have suffered,
the comrades we have lost,

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:07.290
or my father's wrongful death!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.670
York has the lawful claim unto the crown!

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:15.210
I will prove that with my sword today,
on this battlefield!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:19.880
York! York! York! York!

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:24.470
Buckingham, is everything
ready in the woods?

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.930
As you ordered.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.560
Then commence battle.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.690
Keep firing! Don't give the enemy
a moment's respite!

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:43.870
The unexpectedly fierce rain of cannon
fire will soon make them anxious.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.990
Duke Richard!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:46.870
Look there!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.620
The enemy's right wing!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.330
They've moved!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.000
Left, men! Circle around them!

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:02.220
Are you awake, Your Highness?
Please, remain resting.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.470
Where am I?

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.180
Where is my armor?! My sword?!

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.980
No, Your Highness! Please do not leave
this room until the battle is ended.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:17.230
This is Anne's doing!

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.900
Don't end yet, battle!

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.610
Wait for me, York!

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.790
Don't give an inch!

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.960
Let anger govern my heart!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.250
My sword, don't lose your edge yet!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:39.960
An ally?

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.630
No, not an ally!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.100
You're...

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.720
Richard!

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:53.140
You know my name?

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:55.690
I'm sorry, but I don't have time to talk!

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:58.650
Please make way!
I don't want to strike you down!

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:02.860
So, you've thrown in your lot with
Lancaster! I can't let you pass, then!

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:07.870
Damn it!

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.620
Wait! Why won't you fight?!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.290
--Because...
--Are you afraid to die?!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.340
No!

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.150
Richard, I can't fight you because

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.940
I love...

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.580
Richard.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.160
Lie there in shame.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.370
Richard!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.460
Where's our support?!

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.050
Our unit won't last!

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.140
Richard! Curse you!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.600
Look! The enemy fled!

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.770
We've routed them! Crush them now!

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:27.740
Don't let a single Lancastrian escape!
Chase them down and kill them!

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.030
The Lancastrian Prince is escaping!

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.580
Queen Margaret! Please save your--

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.670
You have no allies left.

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:45.800
Do you imagine I fear the leader
of some Yorkist rebels?

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:51.050
Now, guide me, executioner.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:56.430
Murder a queen anointed by God
with those filthy hands of yours.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:04.110
We've captured Margaret! Victory is ours!

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.190
No, the prince is still on the run.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:10.570
"The prince"?! Anne said she
had a double ready, but...

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.610
It can't be!

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:20.120
It will be fine. I can get away.
I can ride a horse better than anyone.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:24.170
Get as far away as you can now, Edward!

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:31.260
Margaret must have given herself
up to let the prince escape.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.300
We'll join in his pursuit!

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:36.970
Anne, don't tell me you took my place!

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.850
It's to guard the blood of Lancaster!

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.560
Is Mother behind this?

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:48.650
She denied me a sword, and now she
wants me to sacrifice my wife to flee?

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:49.440
Who's there?!

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:52.320
Who do you take me for?!

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:03.460
You're Edward of Lancaster.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.420
This voice!

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.630
I'm going to present your
mother with your head.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:08.760
Wait!

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.720
Edward! Why?!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:16.640
Anne?!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:18.560
Richard.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:24.480
Hear me! I am the son of Henry VI,
the rightful King of England!

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:28.270
I am Crown Prince Edward!

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.110
You're the crown prince?!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.740
Run! Run away, Edward!

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.210
Lancaster,

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:46.920
how many times must you make me...?!

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:00.930
I see you haven't turned a hair.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:04.230
I shall endure my fate without a struggle.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:07.150
No matter what that fate may be?

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.360
H-How?

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.110
What are you doing here?

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:20.790
Mother, I'm no longer a child
for you to lead by the hand!

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.910
What foolishness!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:28.750
Sons of York! The prince is still a child!

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.500
He is not even worthy of your hatred!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:34.130
If you seek vengeance, take it on me.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:38.470
It was I who struck off
your father's head!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.890
You can't have forgotten.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:45.810
Your father wept pitifully as he died!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.690
Lancaster!

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:54.780
Oh, I'll never forget how that
conceited rebel died like a worm,

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:57.700
or his miserable, tear-stained head!

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.570
Lancaster!

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:02.990
Or the moment I lopped it off
with my own hands!

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:07.620
My heart still rejoices when I recall it!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.290
When I recall your father's foolish death!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:13.170
Silence! I'll stop your heart
for you right now!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.550
Wait, George!

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:18.470
Killing one who seeks death
would be charity.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:21.350
Say your prayers, prince of Lancaster.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:23.100
Wait! Wait!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.680
Unlike me, the prince is merciful!

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:30.560
He'll pray for York!
Now, pray! Pray, Edward!

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.400
You are going to be king,

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.530
Edward.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:43.280
It will come to war soon.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.830
Who should we side with?

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:47.750
Prince Edward!

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.500
Is anything the matter?!

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.210
King...

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:59.590
Look, Mother! I'll be a splendid king!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:03.010
When I'm king, I'm certain

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:05.270
everyone will look at me.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:20.110
Say something befitting a subject.

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:21.910
What are you saying?

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.830
Kneel, insolent wretches!

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.290
Lustful Edward!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.830
Traitorous George!

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.830
Reprobates born of filthy rebel blood!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:32.670
I am your king!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.970
Once I'm king,

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:41.180
all my wishes will come true.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.970
T-Traitors!

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.810
Edward! Edward!

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.890
Kill me! This instant!

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:53.310
Why won't you kill me, cowards?!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.610
Of course! Richard! Where is he?!

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:58.610
That demon would never
spurn a petitioner for blood.

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:01.700
If you're looking for Richard,
he's in hell now

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:04.490
until he eradicates
the House of Lancaster.

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.370
It hurts. I can't breathe.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.830
Is this the end?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.250
None of my wishes have come true yet.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:18.210
I didn't care about the crown.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:19.960
What I...

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.010
What I really wanted was...

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.890
I had a wish that I wanted to
come true, no matter what it took.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:46.030
Richard, have you come for me?

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.870
Just one last wish.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:55.460
Listen, Richard.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.170
I love you!

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:06.050
At least let it be you.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.890
I want to perish at your hand.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:26.410
Kill me too! Hurry!

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.160
Yes, I'll kill you.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:29.620
Wait!

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.700
We've already done too much. Stop.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:36.080
Why? This woman is the root of it all!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:39.880
That's why death is too good for her.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.970
Margaret, go on living in despair.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:53.390
Edward, my darling son.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:56.730
Why were you killed and I left alone?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:01.190
Kill me! Kill me this instant!
